  "description": "Strings() keys reachable from gen1recomp's game3 (FireRed) runtime: every literal Strings() callsite under src/{core,ui,battle,world}/game3, plus every text value option_rows.lua passes to Strings() through a variable (group and speed-row labels, and what the Letterbox, VideoMode, Orientation, ScreenPosition, FrameCap, VSync, Performance, Zoom, VoidFill and TouchControls label functions return). Language-neutral values those functions also return are left out: numbers and multipliers (FPS caps, tilt angles, 4X-6X FAITHFUL RATIO levels, 59.73HZ/60HZ, FrameCap's \"N (NHZ)\" form). A qid names the FireRed cart's own row for a menu the cart has; the rest are port-added rows. Values that option_rows.lua returns without Strings() (cartLabel: SLOW/MID/FAST, ON/OFF, SHIFT/SET, MONO/STEREO, HELP/LR/L=A) are not reachable and are tracked in docs/upstream-fixes.md. \"Go back to the\\nprevious menu.\" is excluded although the Strings scanner sees it: src/ui/game3/pc_menu.lua wraps it in Strings.source(), which returns the English text, and draw_status_lines prints it without a Strings() lookup.",
